{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"otelgin #5946 #6609 MultipartForm cleanup approach implementation status"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**1. otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** raised an issue regarding context reversal in DataRace for otelgin. The context, stored within the otelgin struct, is reverted after middleware execution to prevent parent middlewares from accessing the span. However, Go routines spawned after a request might still need the span in their context. This discussion was based on [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014).\\n\\n*   Damien believes the current behavior is correct and that users should explicitly pass the current context to spawned Go routines. He cited the collector's pattern of passing context directly outside HTTP requests for processors and exporters as a good example.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** agreed, suggesting that passing necessary values like the span to spawned Go routines is the appropriate solution. He also mentioned OpenTelemetry's pattern of linking spans for asynchronous operations rather than making them child references.\\n\\n**2. otelgin Middleware and Temporary Multi-part Forms**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** brought up an issue where using middleware causes temporary multi-part forms not to be destroyed. This occurs because the instrumentation clones the HTTP request, but the multipart form is not duplicated, preventing proper cleanup. This issue is a historical one, manifesting in otelgin but potentially affecting virtually all HTTP-related middleware.\\n\\n*   References for this issue include:\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k transcript 1 otelgin context revers in datarac damien mathieu rais an issu regard context revers in datarac for otelgin the context store within the otelgin struct is revert after middlewar execut to prevent parent middlewar from access the span howev go routin spawn after a request might still need the span in their context this discuss wa base on http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 damien belief the current behavior is correct and that user should explicit pas the current context to spawn go routin he cite the collector s pattern of pass context direct outsid http request for processor and export a a good exampl tyler yahn agre suggest that pass necessari valu like the span to spawn go routin is the appropri solut he also mention opentelemetri s pattern of link span for asynchron oper rather than make them child refer 2 otelgin middlewar and temporari multi part form damien mathieu brought up an issu where use middlewar caus temporari multi part form not to be destroy this occur becaus the instrument clone the http request but the multipart form is not duplic prevent proper cleanup this issu is a histor one manifest in otelgin but potenti affect virtual all http relat middlewar refer for this issu includ http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"d2762ef7a24b09d4\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.36885742175557623, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.22474120250796606, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7051286, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"873e60b08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:25\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I think this approach could work, but it feels a bit unusual to enforce form parsing in the middleware.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T16:18:27Z\\n\\nHaving to force remove multipart files is a bit unusual too.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:44:13Z\\n\\nI'm probably more in favor of doing the initialization on the original request as well, explicitly handling clean up logic does seem a bit strange\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:49:47Z\\n\\n@dmathieu maybe we should discuss this in the SIG since it might have implications in the other instrumentation modules\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:50:46Z\\n\\nI won't be able to attend this week's meeting (it's the week where it's late for EU). But yes, feel free to bring it there.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-19T18:17:34Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J what are you thoughts on parsing the form in the middleware, the more I think about it, the more that seems to be the better approach, for example what about certain edge cases where down the chain middlewares might want to access the files\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-20T01:52:04Z\\n\\n@akats7 Another option is to save `c.Request` to a variable before calling `c.Request.WithContext(ctx)`. Then, in the defer function, if `c.Request.MultipartForm != nil`, we can reattach the `MultipartForm` to the original request. This way, there won’t be any automatic removing or parsing. If other middlewares handle the form correctly, this approach should work. \\n\\nIn [http/server.go](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41/src/net/http/server.go#L2102), the `ServeHTTP` method is called first, which invokes the Gin handlers/middlewares, and then `finishRequest` is called, which removes the temporary files.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i think this approach could work but it feel a bit unusu to enforc form pars in the middlewar dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t16 18 27z have to forc remov multipart file is a bit unusu too akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 44 13z i m probabl more in favor of do the initi on the origin request a well explicit handl clean up logic doe seem a bit strang akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 49 47z dmathieu mayb we should discus this in the sig sinc it might have implic in the other instrument modul dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 50 46z i won t be abl to attend this week s meet it s the week where it s late for eu but yes feel free to bring it there akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 19t18 17 34z yile j what are you thought on pars the form in the middlewar the more i think about it the more that seem to be the better approach for exampl what about certain edg case where down the chain middlewar might want to access the file yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 20t01 52 04z akats7 anoth option is to save c request to a variabl befor call c request withcontext ctx then in the defer function if c request multipartform nil we can reattach the multipartform to the origin request this way there won t be ani automat remov or pars if other middlewar handl the form correct this approach should work in http server go http github com golang go blob 40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41 src net http server go l2102 the servehttp method is call first which invok the gin handler middlewar and then finishrequest is call which remov the temporari file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"b3dbc649c958ce01\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3497532084712017, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1780881806731453, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75030494, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"However, this approach will also introduce additional side effects, for which there is currently no better solution.  \\n\\n**Impact:**  \\n\\nAssuming our middleware is wrapped in the following manner: `m1(m2(otel-middleware(m3(fn))))`,  \\n\\nwhere `m1` and `m2` internally implement operations such as `request.ParseMultipartForm(1)`. Due to the effect of `RemoveAll` in `otel-middleware`,  \\n\\nthere may be cases where they repeatedly create `request.MultipartForm` resources, resulting in additional memory allocations.\\n\\nOf course, we can also choose not to handle it, but we need to remind users to process `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`.\\n\\n----\\n\\nI'd like to hear your opinions: @akats7 @open-telemetry/go-approvers \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `area: instrumentation`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `bug`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `instrumentation: otelgin`\\n\\n- 2024-11-21T12:21:58Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:45Z · **cross-referenced** by Yiling-J ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T08:06:05Z · **marked_as_duplicate** by dmathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"howev this approach will also introduc addit side effect for which there is current no better solut impact assum our middlewar is wrap in the follow manner m1 m2 otel middlewar m3 fn where m1 and m2 intern implement oper such a request parsemultipartform 1 due to the effect of removeal in otel middlewar there may be case where they repeat creat request multipartform resourc result in addit memori alloc of cours we can also choos not to handl it but we need to remind user to process c request multipartform removeal i d like to hear your opinion akats7 open telemetri go approv sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston timelin 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx area instrument 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx bug 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx instrument otelgin 2024 11 21t12 21 58z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 4588 2025 01 13t13 45 45z cross referenc by yile j http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 2025 07 02t08 06 05z mark _ a _ duplic by dmathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5b39be36d40588b5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.34331831310390915, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.17079616157701308, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74587, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ee5caba072c6dc26\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3373691125561714, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15955016079453066, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75228, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"We should also decide whether to fix this in otelgin only, or to review other middlewares and address the issue there as well if it exists.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-04T00:35:28Z\\n\\n> let’s reach an agreement on how we should fix it\\n\\nWe tend to only need to add the following on the basis of the original main branch:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nc.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()\\n\\n```\\n\\n> We should also decide whether to fix this in otelgin only, or to review other middlewares and address the issue there as well if it exists.\\n\\nIn fact, all middleware based on `*http.Request` has issues whenever a situation like `c.Request.WithContext(c.Request.Context())` occurs, so other components also need to be fixed.\\n\\nHowever, for this current PR, we only need to fix otelgin to keep the PR as minimal as possible. For other middleware, if you are interested, you can also submit fixes in the form of minimal PRs for individual components.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-04T01:19:00Z\\n\\n@flc1125 `RemoveAll()` works for me. I think my original PR already aligns well with the goal, it looks like I just need to resolve the conflicts and make sure the tests pass. Let me confirm agin that we’re all in agreement on this approach. @dmathieu @akats7\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T01:45:42Z\\n\\nSorry just got caught up on this thread. My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data. \\n\\nWhat about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\\nI don't want to stall this issue further but just a thought.\\n\\ncc. @flc1125 @dmathieu  \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T01:53:34Z\\n\\n> Sorry just got caught up on this thread. My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nAgree.\\n\\n> What about making it configurable with an Option, with the default behavior being to clean it up. That way the user can have more control over which middleware cleans up the form data.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist flc1125 2025 11 04t00 35 28z let s reach an agreement on how we should fix it we tend to onli need to add the follow on the basi of the origin main branch go c request multipartform removeal we should also decid whether to fix this in otelgin onli or to review other middlewar and address the issu there a well if it exist in fact all middlewar base on http request ha issu whenev a situat like c request withcontext c request context occur so other compon also need to be fix howev for this current pr we onli need to fix otelgin to keep the pr a minim a possibl for other middlewar if you are interest you can also submit fix in the form of minim pr for individu compon yile j 2025 11 04t01 19 00z flc1125 removeal work for me i think my origin pr alreadi align well with the goal it look like i just need to resolv the conflict and make sure the test pas let me confirm agin that we re all in agreement on this approach dmathieu akats7 akats7 2025 11 10t01 45 42z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data i don t want to stall this issu further but just a thought cc flc1125 dmathieu flc1125 2025 11 10t01 53 34z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data agre what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"3c8bf7e7b452e3f2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32567237664114124, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.14101214091591605, \"vector_similarity\": 0.75654626, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\