Context` method is widely used by middlewares and frameworks, I think they might be able to suggest best practice for this situation.\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-27T12:14:50Z\\n\\n@akats7 It seems I can’t get any help from the Go team. I’m not in favor of parsing the form in the middleware, as this step should be explicitly done by the user. Parsing large forms can consume resources, and the `ParseMultipartForm` function has a `maxMemory` parameter that should also be decided by the user.\\n\\nAfter giving this more thought over the past few days, I believe this is more of a Go design issue. The `WithContext` and `ParseMultipartForm` behavior is implicit, hard to notice, poorly documented, and lacks a clear best practice solution. I think the reattach approach might be better because it’s less aggressive and can likely be safely applied to other OpenTelemetry middlewares facing the same issue. The only downside, compared to `RemoveAll`, is that it relies on other middlewares to also handle `WithContext` and `ParseMultipartForm` correctly. If all middlewares do the right thing, `net/http` should eventually clean up the temporary files automatically.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `CHANGELOG.md` — 2025-11-10T14:01:14Z\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n- Fix issue in `go.opentelemetry.io/contrib/instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin` middleware where temporary files for multipart/form-data were not being removed. (#6609)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-11-10T14:03:40Z\\n\\nClose to reduce distractions.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-11-10T14:03:54Z\\n\\nClose to reduce distractions.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:20:30Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i haven t test yet but i think it should work howev i m consid open an issu in go to get their suggest sinc it s close relat to the http packag and the withcontext method is wide use by middlewar and framework i think they might be abl to suggest best practic for this situat yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 27t12 14 50z akats7 it seem i can t get ani help from the go team i m not in favor of pars the form in the middlewar a this step should be explicit done by the user pars larg form can consum resourc and the parsemultipartform function ha a maxmemori paramet that should also be decid by the user after give this more thought over the past few day i believ this is more of a go design issu the withcontext and parsemultipartform behavior is implicit hard to notic poor document and lack a clear best practic solut i think the reattach approach might be better becaus it s less aggress and can like be safe appli to other opentelemetri middlewar face the same issu the onli downsid compar to removeal is that it reli on other middlewar to also handl withcontext and parsemultipartform correct if all middlewar do the right thing net http should eventu clean up the temporari file automat flc1125 on changelog md 2025 11 10t14 01 14z suggest fix issu in go opentelemetri io contrib instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin middlewar where temporari file for multipart form data were not be remov 6609 flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 11 10t14 03 40z close to reduc distract flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 11 10t14 03 54z close to reduc distract flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 20 30z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ebe0290167cd7c66\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.30975931472611096, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12247412103730136, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7467581, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:36: File removed: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n```\\n\\n----\\n\\nCurrently, I cannot determine whether this is a flaw in Go itself or if users are required to manually execute `RemoveAll()`. I have tried submitting [this issue](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455) to the official Go team to see if there will be any updates.\\n\\nThe following situations exist (tested and confirmed):\\n\\n1. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, but did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will be unable to delete the files;\\n\\n2. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, and manually called `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files;\\n\\n3. We executed `request.WithContext()` after executing `request.ParseMultipartForm,` and did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-03T13:24:52Z\\n\\nGiven that this [issue](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946#issuecomment-3028290240) currently lacks an official solution from the [Go team](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455), we need to find an appropriate workaround ourselves.\\n\\nMy suggestion is to proceed with the solution proposed in this [PR](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609) (also the consistent approach suggested by @zihuyishi and @akats7).  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 36 file remov var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 current i can not determin whether this is a flaw in go itself or if user are requir to manual execut removeal i have tri submit this issu http github com golang go issu 74455 to the offici go team to see if there will be ani updat the follow situat exist test and confirm 1 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform but did not manual call removeal on the new request it will be unabl to delet the file 2 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform and manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the file 3 we execut request withcontext after execut request parsemultipartform and did not manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the 