evaluate whether increasing it will have any impact when wrapping this middleware with an outer layer.\\n\\nI think the cause of the issue is when we replace the request we stop the form from being fully initialised on the original request, so at the end of the (original) request lifecycle, there’s nothing for the server to cleanup.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-02T15:23:47Z\\n\\nI don't think this issue exists only in the Gin framework, but rather in all `http.Server` implementations.\\n\\nThe following is a simplified version of the experimental results:\\n\\n```go\\n\\nfunc TestHTTPRequest(t *testing.T) {\\n\\n\\treq := &http.Request{}\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"zihuyishi 2025 07 02t09 37 44z i think we should manual remov it who creat new request should cleanup golang defer func if c request multipartform nil c request multipartform removeal akats7 2025 07 02t09 40 40z i think we should manual remov it who creat new request should cleanup defer func if c request multipartform nil c request multipartform removeal i m fine with this i think this is just the path of least resist then we d also have to explicit pars the form in the middlewar it seem flc1125 2025 07 02t10 01 01z i m fine with this i think this is just the path of least resist then we d also have to explicit pars the form in the middlewar it seem yes this solut is feasibl i m just tri to understand whi this issu occur at the under level in addit it is necessari to evalu whether increas it will have ani impact when wrap this middlewar with an outer layer akats7 2025 07 02t10 06 33z i m fine with this i think this is just the path of least resist then we d also have to explicit pars the form in the middlewar it seem yes this solut is feasibl i m just tri to understand whi this issu occur at the under level in addit it is necessari to evalu whether increas it will have ani impact when wrap this middlewar with an outer layer i think the caus of the issu is when we replac the request we stop the form 