t a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data i don t want to stall this issu further but just a thought cc flc1125 dmathieu flc1125 2025 11 10t01 53 34z sorri just got caught up on this thread my onli concern with removeal is on the off chanc that a middlewar further up the chain still expect access to the form data agre what about make it configur with an option with the default behavior be to clean it up that way the user can have more control over which middlewar clean up the form data\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"3c8bf7e7b452e3f2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3545067352419792, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1661668789171132, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7939664, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"However, this approach will also introduce additional side effects, for which there is currently no better solution.  \\n\\n**Impact:**  \\n\\nAssuming our middleware is wrapped in the following manner: `m1(m2(otel-middleware(m3(fn))))`,  \\n\\nwhere `m1` and `m2` internally implement operations such as `request.ParseMultipartForm(1)`. Due to the effect of `RemoveAll` in `otel-middleware`,  \\n\\nthere may be cases where they repeatedly create `request.MultipartForm` resources, resulting in additional memory allocations.\\n\\nOf course, we can also choose not to handle it, but we need to remind users to process `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`.\\n\\n----\\n\\nI'd like to hear your opinions: @akats7 @open-telemetry/go-approvers \\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-ISSUE-01]\\n\\n# Issue: Using otelgin.Middleware will cause temporary MultipartForm files not to be destroyed. (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#5946)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946  \\n\\n**Author**: zacklpx  \\n\\n**Created**: 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **Updated**: 2025-07-03T13:28:05Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Labels**: bug, area: instrumentation, instrumentation: otelgin  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `area: instrumentation`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `bug`\\n\\n- 2024-07-25T03:50:39Z · **labeled** by zacklpx `instrumentation: otelgin`\\n\\n- 2024-11-21T12:21:58Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/4588\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:45Z · **cross-referenced** by Yiling-J ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609\\n\\n- 2025-07-02T08:06:05Z · **marked_as_duplicate** by dmathieu\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"howev this approach will also introduc addit side effect for which there is current no better solut impact assum our middlewar is wrap in the follow manner m1 m2 otel middlewar m3 fn where m1 and m2 intern implement oper such a request parsemultipartform 1 due to the effect of removeal in otel middlewar there may be case where they repeat creat request multipartform resourc result in addit memori alloc of cours we can also choos not to handl it but we need to remind user to process c request multipartform removeal i d like to hear your opinion akats7 open telemetri go approv sourc id src issu 01 issu use otelgin middlewar will caus temporari multipartform file not to be destroy open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 5946 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 author zacklpx creat 2024 07 25t03 50 39z updat 2025 07 03t13 28 05z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open label bug area instrument instrument otelgin mileston timelin 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx area instrument 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx bug 2024 07 25t03 50 39z label by zacklpx instrument otelgin 2024 11 21t12 21 58z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 4588 2025 01 13t13 45 45z cross referenc by yile j http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 2025 07 02t08 06 05z mark _ a _ duplic by dmathieu\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5b39be36d40588b5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3427326014483288, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.15869211635475544, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7721604, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:33: File modified: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n    gin2_test.go:36: File removed: /var/folders/9q/lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn/T/TestHTTP124433030/001/multipart-643567324\\n\\n```\\n\\n----\\n\\nCurrently, I cannot determine whether this is a flaw in Go itself or if users are required to manually execute `RemoveAll()`. I have tried submitting [this issue](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455) to the official Go team to see if there will be any updates.\\n\\nThe following situations exist (tested and confirmed):\\n\\n1. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, but did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will be unable to delete the files;\\n\\n2. We executed `request.WithContext()` before executing `request.ParseMultipartForm`, and manually called `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files;\\n\\n3. We executed `request.WithContext()` after executing `request.ParseMultipartForm,` and did not manually call `RemoveAll` on the new Request—it will delete the files.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-07-03T13:24:52Z\\n\\nGiven that this [issue](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946#issuecomment-3028290240) currently lacks an official solution from the [Go team](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455), we need to find an appropriate workaround ourselves.\\n\\nMy suggestion is to proceed with the solution proposed in this [PR](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609) (also the consistent approach suggested by @zihuyishi and @akats7).  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 33 file modifi var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 gin2 _ test go 36 file remov var folder 9q lfpvvb251dv7bj4tqlq8bgpm0000gn t testhttp124433030 001 multipart 643567324 current i can not determin whether this is a flaw in go itself or if user are requir to manual execut removeal i have tri submit this issu http github com golang go issu 74455 to the offici go team to see if there will be ani updat the follow situat exist test and confirm 1 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform but did not manual call removeal on the new request it will be unabl to delet the file 2 we execut request withcontext befor execut request parsemultipartform and manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the file 3 we execut request withcontext after execut request parsemultipartform and did not manual call removeal on the new request it will delet the file flc1125 2025 07 03t13 24 52z given that this issu http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 issuecom 3028290240 current lack an offici solut from the go team http github com golang go issu 74455 we need to find an appropri workaround ourselv my suggest is to proceed with the solut propos in this pr http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 also the consist approach suggest by zihuyishi and akats7\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"id\": \"5af8802d20a0e988\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3307492258779691, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13322863696852735, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7916306, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8751eb948a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/issues/opentelemetry-go-contrib-5946.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 16121, \"chunk_count\": 10, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:14\", \"token_count\": 5002, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-13T15:31:16Z\\n\\nI prefer using `require.NoError` because it ensures that no additional information distracts me when a test has already failed. I also searched the codebase and seems that both `require` and `assert` are used, and `require.NoError` appears more.\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T15:35:44Z\\n\\nIt's hard to say, but in all cases, regardless of how many middlewares are chained, temporary files should be removed. I didn't check the return error of `RemoveAll` here, which aligns with the behavior in both Go's [`http` package](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e/src/net/http/server.go#L1727) and [echo-contrib](https://github.com/labstack/echo-contrib/pull/90). I believe each middleware should independently attempt to remove temporary files.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 117) — 2025-01-13T16:20:13Z\\n\\nsee: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609#issuecomment-2587572600\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gintrace.go` — 2025-01-14T08:12:17Z\\n\\nRather than ignoring an error here, how about passing it to the otel error handler?\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\terr := c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\totel.Handle(err)\\n\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\n```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/test/gintrace_test.go` — 2025-01-14T08:13:50Z\\n\\nI think what @flc1125 meant here is that you don't necessarily need to use `AbortWithError` (which also can return an error but ignores it), but instead call `require.NoError` here.\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\trequire.NoError(err)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 13t15 31 16z i prefer use requir noerror becaus it ensur that no addit inform distract me when a test ha alreadi fail i also search the codebas and seem that both requir and assert are use and requir noerror appear more yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t15 35 44z it s hard to say but in all case regardless of how mani middlewar are chain temporari file should be remov i didn t check the return error of removeal here which align with the behavior in both go s http packag http github com golang go blob 44a6f817ea0fbeb3ba4aa398794c4e80dba13b1e src net http server go l1727 and echo contrib http github com labstack echo contrib pull 90 i believ each middlewar should independ attempt to remov temporari file flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 117 2025 01 13t16 20 13z see http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 issuecom 2587572600 dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gintrac go 2025 01 14t08 12 17z rather than ignor an error here how about pass it to the otel error handler suggest err c request multipartform removeal if err nil otel handl err dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin test gintrac _ test go 2025 01 14t08 13 50z i think what flc1125 meant here is that you don t necessarili need to use abortwitherror which also can return an error but ignor it but instead call requir noerror here suggest requir noerror err\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"a6289f2135157364\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32853849925894485, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.13449588465563553, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7813046, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +95 / -0 across 3 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:44Z · **review_requested** by Yiling-J\\n\\n- 2025-01-13T13:45:57Z · **review_requested** by github-actions[bot]\\n\\n- 2025-01-22T15:54:04Z · **cross-referenced** by Yiling-J ← https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382\\n\\n- 2025-07-03T13:24:53Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946\\n\\n- 2025-11-03T09:18:09Z · **cross-referenced** by pellared ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648\\n\\n- 2025-11-11T14:00:20Z · **cross-referenced** by flc1125 ← https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 author yile j creat 2025 01 13t13 45 43z updat 2025 11 13t01 26 12z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state open branch fix gin _ multipartform main chang 95 0 across 3 file label mileston timelin 2025 01 13t13 45 44z review _ request by yile j 2025 01 13t13 45 57z review _ request by github action bot 2025 01 22t15 54 04z cross referenc by yile j http github com golang go issu 71382 2025 07 03t13 24 53z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 2025 11 03t09 18 09z cross referenc by pellar http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 2025 11 11t14 00 20z cross referenc by flc1125 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"d941c8802823bfb6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3227947724847554, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12056023926393629, \"vector_similarity\": 0.79467535, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I don’t think this is the expected result; in any case—whether it’s middleware or something else—it should be able to retrieve the file again.\\n\\nI think we may need to investigate this issue further.\\n\\n**flc1125** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T13:59:33Z\\n\\nBased on this PR, I’ve provided a prototype reference: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8161\\n\\n@dmathieu @akats7, take a look and see how it works if we adjust it according to the prototype.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-11T15:42:57Z\\n\\n@flc1125 can you clarify which behavior you’re referring to as incorrect, are you referring to \\n\\n```\\n\\nrequire.ErrorIs(t, err, fs.ErrNotExist)\\n\\n```\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T01:28:14Z\\n\\nI thought we had already agreed on the `RemoveAll` approach? Naturally, if you call RemoveAll, the temporary files are deleted and can’t be accessed afterward. Since this happens during the middleware’s return phase, I’d expect that most middlewares wouldn’t read the multipart form at that point anyway. I’m not sure if the implications of RemoveAll were discussed in the SIG meeting, but it might be worth confirming.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin_test.go` (line 512) — 2025-11-12T10:24:52Z\\n\\n@flc1125 I’m still not clear on the result you’re referring to, the result aligns to my understanding of what we’ve discussed.\\n\\nAlso I’m not sure if your prototype fix would work, I think it still doesn’t address the core issue which is that when we originally set c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx) with an unparsed form the http server won’t know to clean it up. I don’t think Cloning the request solves that.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i don t think this is the expect result in ani case whether it s middlewar or someth els it should be abl to retriev the file again i think we may need to investig this issu further flc1125 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t13 59 33z base on this pr i ve provid a prototyp refer http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8161 dmathieu akats7 take a look and see how it work if we adjust it accord to the prototyp akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 11t15 42 57z flc1125 can you clarifi which behavior you re refer to a incorrect are you refer to requir errori t err f errnotexist yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t01 28 14z i thought we had alreadi agre on the removeal approach natur if you call removeal the temporari file are delet and can t be access afterward sinc this happen dure the middlewar s return phase i d expect that most middlewar wouldn t read the multipart form at that point anyway i m not sure if the implic of removeal were discuss in the sig meet but it might be worth confirm akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin _ test go line 512 2025 11 12t10 24 52z flc1125 i m still not clear on the result you re refer to the result align to my understand of what we ve discuss also i m not sure if your prototyp fix would work i think it still doesn t address the core issu which is that when we origin set c request c request withcontext ctx with an unpars form the http server won t know to clean it up i don t think clone the request solv that sourc id src pr 01 pull request fix otelgin remov multipartform temporari file open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"ee5caba072c6dc26\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3215130416691242, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11549328809874891, \"vector_similarity\": 0.8022258, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"```\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T08:21:31Z\\n\\nWouldn't we be fixing this rather more easily with the following:\\n\\n```suggestion\\n\\n\\t\\tc.Request = c.Request.Clone(ctx)\\n\\n```\\n\\n[WithContext](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.WithContext) performs a shallow clone, and therefore doesn't clone the multipart form.\\n\\nHowever, [Clone](https://pkg.go.dev/net/http#Request.Clone) performs a deep copy, and makes an explicit clone of [MultipartForm](https://cs.opensource.google/go/go/+/refs/tags/go1.23.4:src/net/http/request.go;l=406).\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:39:53Z\\n\\nThe problem here is, go http request will call MultipartForm.RemoveAll() automatically when request finishes. However, the otelgin middleware creates a new request, and temporary files will be stored in this new request's MultipartForm field. Unfortunately, no one is calling MultipartForm.RemoveAll() on this new request.\\n\\nA deep clone wouldn’t resolve the problem because the MultipartForm is also copied. A shallow clone might seem like it should work since the MultipartForm field is shared, but it doesn’t. This is because the MultipartForm field is lazily initialized—it’s only assigned a value when you [parse the form](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d/src/net/http/request.go#L1403). As a result, in the middleware, the field is nil.\\n\\nRelated issues: https://github.com/golang/go/issues/58809, https://github.com/labstack/echo/issues/2413\\n\\nI think other OpenTelemetry middlewares, such as otelmux and otelehco, might also have the same issue.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T14:55:45Z\\n\\nWhat if we parse the form before making the new request?\\n\\nWouldn't we share the object then?\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T15:31:10Z\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t08 21 31z wouldn t we be fix this rather more easili with the follow suggest c request c request clone ctx withcontext http pkg go dev net http request withcontext perform a shallow clone and therefor doesn t clone the multipart form howev clone http pkg go dev net http request clone perform a deep copi and make an explicit clone of multipartform http c opensourc googl go go ref tag go1 23 4 src net http request go l 406 yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 39 53z the problem here is go http request will call multipartform removeal automat when request finish howev the otelgin middlewar creat a new request and temporari file will be store in this new request s multipartform field unfortun no one is call multipartform removeal on this new request a deep clone wouldn t resolv the problem becaus the multipartform is also copi a shallow clone might seem like it should work sinc the multipartform field is share but it doesn t this is becaus the multipartform field is lazili initi it s onli assign a valu when you pars the form http github com golang go blob 6da16013ba4444e0d71540f68279f0283a92d05d src net http request go l1403 a a result in the middlewar the field is nil relat issu http github com golang go issu 58809 http github com labstack echo issu 2413 i think other opentelemetri middlewar such a otelmux and otelehco might also have the same issu dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t14 55 45z what if we pars the form befor make the new request wouldn t we share the object then yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t15 31 10z\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"0b66ff59ca7469a0\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31809850166912423, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11549328809874891, \"vector_similarity\": 0.790844, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I think this approach could work, but it feels a bit unusual to enforce form parsing in the middleware.\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T16:18:27Z\\n\\nHaving to force remove multipart files is a bit unusual too.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:44:13Z\\n\\nI'm probably more in favor of doing the initialization on the original request as well, explicitly handling clean up logic does seem a bit strange\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:49:47Z\\n\\n@dmathieu maybe we should discuss this in the SIG since it might have implications in the other instrumentation modules\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:50:46Z\\n\\nI won't be able to attend this week's meeting (it's the week where it's late for EU). But yes, feel free to bring it there.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-19T18:17:34Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J what are you thoughts on parsing the form in the middleware, the more I think about it, the more that seems to be the better approach, for example what about certain edge cases where down the chain middlewares might want to access the files\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-20T01:52:04Z\\n\\n@akats7 Another option is to save `c.Request` to a variable before calling `c.Request.WithContext(ctx)`. Then, in the defer function, if `c.Request.MultipartForm != nil`, we can reattach the `MultipartForm` to the original request. This way, there won’t be any automatic removing or parsing. If other middlewares handle the form correctly, this approach should work. \\n\\nIn [http/server.go](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41/src/net/http/server.go#L2102), the `ServeHTTP` method is called first, which invokes the Gin handlers/middlewares, and then `finishRequest` is called, which removes the temporary files.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i think this approach could work but it feel a bit unusu to enforc form pars in the middlewar dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t16 18 27z have to forc remov multipart file is a bit unusu too akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 44 13z i m probabl more in favor of do the initi on the origin request a well explicit handl clean up logic doe seem a bit strang akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 49 47z dmathieu mayb we should discus this in the sig sinc it might have implic in the other instrument modul dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 50 46z i won t be abl to attend this week s meet it s the week where it s late for eu but yes feel free to bring it there akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 19t18 17 34z yile j what are you thought on pars the form in the middlewar the more i think about it the more that seem to be the better approach for exampl what about certain edg case where down the chain middlewar might want to access the file yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 20t01 52 04z akats7 anoth option is to save c request to a variabl befor call c request withcontext ctx then in the defer function if c request multipartform nil we can reattach the multipartform to the origin request this way there won t be ani automat remov or pars if other middlewar handl the form correct this approach should work in http server go http github com golang go blob 40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41 src net http server go l2102 the servehttp method is call first which invok the gin handler middlewar and then finishrequest is call which remov the temporari file\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"b3dbc649c958ce01\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31405000247251735, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.10915908924645337, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7921288, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8755686e8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 27213, \"chunk_count\": 18, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:09\", \"token_count\": 9176, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"I would lean towards the solution proposed by the SIG: only support configurability when users explicitly request it. After all, enabling configurability after `RemoveAll()` is an operation that ensures both extensibility compatibility and backward compatibility.\\n\\n@akats7 @dmathieu \\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T02:01:52Z\\n\\nAh gotcha, didn't see that that was mentioned. I'm good on holding off until it's explicitly requested.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**akats7** — 2025-11-10T04:27:26Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J I think we're good to resolve the conflicts and close this out, thanks!\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T11:58:48Z\\n\\nI’ve resolved the conflicts, and the otelgin package tests passed on my machine @flc1125 @dmathieu @akats7 \\n\\n---\\n\\n**flc1125** — 2025-11-10T14:02:53Z\\n\\nCould you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Yiling-J** — 2025-11-10T15:21:14Z\\n\\n> Could you add the corresponding unit tests for this scenario?\\n\\n> \\n\\n> > My only concern with RemoveAll is on the off chance that a middleware further up the chain still expect access to the form data.\\n\\nI’ve added more details to the test case, it now includes two extra middlewares, one upstream and one downstream, to demonstrate what happens when `RemoveAll` is called in the otel middleware. The behavior is correct to me, but let’s confirm that we all agree it’s the expected one.\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-01]\\n\\n# Pull Request: fix(otelgin): remove multipartform temporary file (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#6609)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609  \\n\\n**Author**: Yiling-J  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-01-13T13:45:43Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-13T01:26:12Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: open  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/gin_multipartform` → `main`  \\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i would lean toward the solut propos by the sig onli support configur when user explicit request it after all enabl configur after removeal is an oper that ensur both extens compat and backward compat akats7 dmathieu akats7 2025 11 10t02 01 52z ah gotcha didn t see that that wa mention i m good on hold off until it s explicit request aka